 ## Background
-The method was developed for the "Smoker" application, a real-time smoke volume rendering system [S1, unofficial]. It was presented in a master's thesis by Sowinski in 2012 [S1, unofficial]. The pipeline was chosen to provide a flexible framework allowing runtime switching between different rendering strategies without re-initializing the smoke volume, facilitating comparison of approaches under identical configurations [S1, unofficial].
+The Fragment List-Based Rendering Pipeline was developed as part of the "Smoker" application for real-time smoke volume rendering. It was presented in a master's thesis by Dirk Sowinski in 2012 [S1, unofficial]. The method was chosen to address the limitations of raytracing techniques, specifically self-intersection and global intersection problems, while maintaining accuracy through a four-stage shader-based pipeline [S1, unofficial].
 
